---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import StoreCTA from '../components/StoreCTA.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
const steps = [
  { number: '01', title: 'Shape a profile.', description: 'Explore depth, time, gas mixes, and ascent and descent rates.' },
  { number: '02', title: 'Look beneath the curve.', description: 'Adjust gradient factors and explore open circuit, CCR, and bailout profiles.' },
  { number: '03', title: 'Read the details.', description: 'Follow decompression stops, tissue loading, and time to surface in one place.' },
];
---

<Layout title="DiveHub — See the dive. Understand the theory." description="Explore OC and CCR profiles, Bühlmann ZH-L16C with gradient factors, and tissue visualization in DiveHub. An educational app for iPhone and iPad.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> A deeper understanding</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">See the dive.<br />Understand<br /><span>the theory.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">Explore dive profiles, decompression stops, and tissue loading. Bring the theory into view with DiveHub.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <StoreCTA />
          <a class="hero-explore" href="#features">Explore the app <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="platform-note">For iPhone and iPad</p>
        <div class="hero-education">
          <span class="note-mark" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
          <p>Built for education and simulation.<br /><a href="#educational-use">Not for planning or executing real dives.</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-visual">
        <div class="visual-topline"><span>PROFILE / TISSUES / STOPS</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></div>
        <div class="profile-stage">
          <svg class="depth-lines" viewBox="0 0 600 600" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
              <path d="M30 130c120-140 340-80 450 45s100 235-45 315S95 510 55 390s140-160 230-100 70 150-20 150" />
              <path d="M5 100c135-155 375-95 500 55s115 275-45 365S55 550 20 410s150-195 260-130 90 185-20 200" />
              <path d="M60 165c95-120 285-60 385 45s70 200-40 260S140 465 95 375s110-130 180-80 50 110-20 115" />
              <path d="M95 205c80-85 220-50 300 35s35 145-45 185-180 15-210-60 80-100 125-60" />
              <path d="M-25 65c145-165 415-115 565 60s125 325-60 425S20 590-10 430" />
            </g>
          </svg>
          <div class="screen-frame screen-secondary"><img src="/images/ccr-profile.webp" alt="DiveHub CCR profile with bailout, decompression stops, and tissue saturation visualization" width="460" height="995" decoding="async" /></div>
          <div class="screen-frame screen-primary"><img src="/images/oc-profile.webp" alt="DiveHub open circuit multi-gas profile showing a depth curve, gas switches, and tissue saturation" width="460" height="995" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /></div>
          <div class="visual-tag"><span class="tag-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> OC + CCR</div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><span>Actual DiveHub interfaces</span><span class="caption-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>One clearer picture</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="capability-strip" aria-label="Core capabilities">
        <p><span>MODEL</span>Bühlmann ZH-L16C</p>
        <p><span>CONTROL</span>Custom gradient factors</p>
        <p><span>PERSPECTIVE</span>Open circuit &amp; CCR</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section id="features" class="features section container" aria-labelledby="features-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Made visible</p>
        <h2 id="features-title">More than numbers.<br />A picture you can explore.</h2>
        <p>See how a profile, its gases, and its decompression model connect. The details stay close to the bigger picture.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card profile-card">
          <div class="feature-copy"><span class="feature-index">01 / VISUALIZE</span><h3>Follow the whole profile.</h3><p>Gas switches, decompression stops, and tissue saturation — brought together in a visual workspace.</p></div>
          <div class="profile-crop"><img src="/images/oc-profile.webp" alt="The OC profile chart and colorful tissue saturation view in DiveHub" width="460" height="995" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
          <span class="image-caption">OPEN CIRCUIT PROFILE / ACTUAL APP VIEW</span>
        </article>
        <div class="feature-side">
          <article class="feature-card model-card">
            <span class="feature-index">02 / UNDERSTAND</span>
            <div class="model-display" aria-hidden="true"><span>ZH</span><span>L16C<span class="model-dot">.</span></span></div>
            <h3>A familiar model. Room to explore.</h3><p>Bühlmann ZH-L16C with customizable GF Low and GF High.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-card circuit-card">
            <span class="feature-index">03 / EXPLORE</span>
            <div class="circuit-display" aria-hidden="true"><span>OC</span><span class="circuit-connector">↔</span><span>CCR</span></div>
            <h3>Two ways to see the theory.</h3><p>Open circuit multi-gas profiles and closed circuit rebreather support, including bailout planning concepts.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="how-it-works" class="workflow-section section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="container workflow-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">From inputs to insight</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Explore. Adjust.<br />See what changes.</h2><p>A visual way to study the relationships behind decompression.</p></div>
          <ol class="workflow-steps">
            {steps.map((step) => <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">{step.number}</span><div><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.description}</p></div></li>)}
          </ol>
        </div>
        <figure class="workflow-visual">
          <div class="workflow-screen settings-screen"><img src="/images/settings.webp" alt="DiveHub settings showing customizable gradient factors for decompression and CCR bailout" width="460" height="995" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
          <div class="workflow-screen ndl-screen"><img src="/images/ndl-calculator.webp" alt="DiveHub NDL calculator with depth and gas inputs, END, gas density, and gradient factor settings" width="460" height="995" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
          <figcaption>Real controls. A more tangible understanding.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="tools-section section container" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
      <div class="tools-panel">
        <div class="tools-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Beyond the profile</p><h2 id="tools-title">Keep the details<br />in the picture.</h2><p>Explore equivalent narcotic depth, gas density, and time to surface. DiveHub also supports wireless Nitrox analyzers.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/divehub-multi-dive-tool/id6756101582">See the full feature list <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <figure class="analyzer-visual"><img src="/images/nitrox-analyzer.webp" alt="DiveHub Oxygen Analyzer interface displaying a connected wireless Nitrox analyzer" width="460" height="995" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Wireless Nitrox analyzer support</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="faq" class="faq-section section container" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A few things to know</p><h2 id="faq-title">Before you explore.</h2></div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details id="educational-use" open>
          <summary>Can I use DiveHub to plan a real dive?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <div><p>No. DiveHub is for education and simulation only. It does not include all the features or account for all the factors required for safe, real-world dive planning. It is not a substitute for professional training, dive computers, or planning tools.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/divehub-multi-dive-tool/id6756101582">Read the full App Store safety notice <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </details>
        <details><summary>Which devices can I use?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>DiveHub is available for iPhone and iPad. Visit the App Store for the current system requirements and device compatibility.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Which decompression model does it use?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>DiveHub implements Bühlmann ZH-L16C with customizable gradient factors. It supports open circuit multi-gas profiles and CCR profiles with bailout planning concepts.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Where can I find privacy information?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Read our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for the app’s data practices and contact information.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I get help or share feedback?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Visit <a href="/support/">Support</a> for contact details and the information to include when reporting an issue.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="download-section container" aria-labelledby="download-title">
      <div class="download-panel">
        <img class="download-icon" src="/images/app-icon.webp" alt="" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
        <p class="eyebrow">DiveHub / iPhone + iPad</p><h2 id="download-title">Take a closer look.</h2>
        <p>Make decompression theory a little more tangible.</p><StoreCTA />
        <span class="download-note">For education and simulation only.</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
